In article <1n5np5INNbph@shelley.u.washington.edu> harmonix@stein.u.washington.edu (Chaz Stevens) writes:
>	A related question:  I've seen to IBM PC versions of NetHack 3.1.0
>floating around, one that states it is for the IBM PC, the other stating that
>it is for an IBM 386.  Are both of these actually the same?

	My personal opinion is to stay away from the 386 one.  No offense to
the person who compiled it.  It has it's advantages...namely, it doesn't have
the Moon Phase bug.  But it has a ton of other bugs that the other version
doesn't have.  Plus, all those complaints about PC nethack grinding the heck
out of people's drives...it's only on this version.
	The other version runs fine on ANY machine.  Well, it may be slow on
old machines.  But it works just peachy on my 386.  And this version has a
working Wizard mode.  :)  The one which doesn't say for 386 only is the
OFFICIAL release of nethack.

